# <%= current_page.data.title %>

The CJS Common Platform (CPP) supports the criminal courts in England and Wales. It is a distinct platform with its own access, deployment and operational processes.

New joiners should read and follow the [onboarding](onboarding/index.html) process to obtain access.

## Service lifecycle

Follow the lifecycle stages in order when bringing a new component onto CPP:

1. [Onboarding](onboarding/index.html): obtain personal access and complete [service onboarding](onboarding/service.html) to agree ownership, dependencies and the first target stack.
2. [Starting a new component](new-component/index.html): create the repository, configure the build, provision dependencies, deploy to non-live and validate the service.
3. [Path to Live](path-to-live/index.html): prepare release evidence and deploy through PRP and PRD with Crime Release Management.
4. [Live service](live-service/index.html): check environment availability and outbound network configuration for running services.

## Platform reference

Use these sections throughout the lifecycle:

- [Architecture](architecture/index.html): platform structure, terminology and the published [architecture model](https://hmcts.github.io/cp-c4-architecture/).
- [Tools and configuration](tools-and-configuration/index.html): service versions, deployment configuration and shared platform tooling.
- [Helm charts](helm-charts/index.html): the shared chart catalogue and how to use and customise charts.
- [Standards](standards/index.html): shared platform services, including [CPP Artifactory](standards/artifactory/index.html) for publishing and resolving artefacts.
